Package: mask
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://mask.branchead.com/
Description: PII pseudonymization gateway for local and cloud LLMs
 mask sits between a client and an LLM API and replaces the personal data it
 detects (names, addresses, phone numbers, cards, and your own dictionary
 terms) with placeholders, then restores the answer on the way back. The model
 only ever sees the placeholders.
 .
 The gateway is started by a person from their own terminal, because that
 terminal is where the operator token for /admin is printed. This package
 therefore installs a binary, a man page and the documents, not a service:
 there is no enabled daemon, no open port, and no configuration file written
 behind your back. The config holds your upstream API key, so it belongs in
 ~/.config/mask/mask.toml with mode 600, outside any checkout that a coding
 agent can read. See /usr/share/doc/mask/mask.toml.example.
